  "narrative": "I assessed the twelve newly delivered discovery results using the run's practical benchmark of roughly 0.10 absolute dependency-score units. All conclusions are dataset-level associations only; independent validation is not available because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. Direction interpretation remains: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means weaker dependency. Interaction estimates are effect-modification contrasts, not stratum main effects.\n\nThe main new positive result is H277. PTEN loss remains associated with stronger STAT3 dependency within MYC-expression-high lines, with a large signed estimate (+0.283, 95% CI +0.211 to +0.354), well above the practical threshold and precisely estimated. This is a context-restricted persistence result for the established PTEN/STAT3 association, not a new causal or generalizable claim. I accept it and close the investigation.\n\nH278 supports specificity of the SMARCA4-SMARCA2 relationship. SMARCA4 loss shows no meaningful association with DHX9 dependency (signed estimate -0.006, 95% CI -0.025 to +0.014); the interval is narrow and entirely below the practical threshold. I reject the hypothesized SMARCA4-DHX9 association, which strengthens the interpretation that the SMARCA4 effect in this dataset is paralog-specific rather than a broad RNA/DNA helicase or housekeeping vulnerability.\n\nH273-H276 retest driver-self dependency after excluding common bypass driver alterations. BRAF V600E among KRAS-wild-type lines, KRAS mutation among BRAF-wild-type lines, EGFR amplification among KRAS/BRAF-wild-type lines, and ERBB2 amplification among KRAS/EGFR-wild-type lines all produce small estimates with intervals well below the practical threshold and not supporting the hypothesized stronger driver-self dependency. I reject these directional claims, which strengthens the prior conclusion that the tested driver markers are not strong driver-self dependency markers in this resource, even when common co-alterations are excluded. These remain negative dataset-level findings, not evidence that such dependencies are absent in other contexts.\n\nThe interaction results are mostly null or inconclusive. H264 (hypoxia-high modification of CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency) rejects the pre-specified positive interaction: signed estimate -0.028, 95% CI -0.113 to +0.057. The positive side is below the practical threshold; the negative side includes a possible moderate opposite interaction, but it is not the registered hypothesis, the point estimate is small, and given multiplicity I do not pursue it. H265, H266, and H267 reject IFN-gamma-high effect modification for SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, TP53-loss USP7, and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependencies: all are near zero with intervals below the practical threshold. H269 similarly rejects IFN-gamma-high effect modification for CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency, although, as with H264, the lower interval bound permits a possible moderate opposite interaction that is not supported as the registered direction and is not pursued.\n\nH268 is the only interaction I leave unresolved. IFN-gamma-high lines may increase MSI-high WRN dependency contrast, but the signed estimate is only +0.051 with a wide 95% CI from -0.009 to +0.111. The interval crosses both null and the practical threshold, so the data are insufficient to accept or decisively reject a meaningful interaction. I close this low-priority ambiguity because the validation budget is exhausted and the point estimate is below the benchmark.\n\nTo target remaining scientific ambiguities, I registered three discovery-only follow-ups: CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency among MTAP-wild-type lines to test genomic-co-deletion confounding; KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency among STK11-intact lines to test robustness against a common lung co-alteration context; and MSI-high WRN dependency among low-mutation-burden lines to test robustness outside the high-TMB context. These are intended to clarify specificity and possible co-alteration confounding, not to establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 appraise decisions: validation budget exhausted; no validation requested. Practical dependency-score benchmark ~0.10 absolute units. H277 accepted as PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency in MYC-high stratum (+0.283, CI +0.211 to +0.354). H278 rejected, supporting SMARCA4 loss specificity for SMARCA2 rather than DHX9. H273-H276 reject driver-self dependency even after excluding common co-drivers. H264-H267, H269 mostly reject IFN/hypoxia interaction hypotheses; H268 unresolved/closed because IFN-high WRN interaction +0.051 (CI -0.009 to +0.111) is not decisive. Registered new discovery follow-ups: MTAP-wild-type CDKN2A/MDM2, STK11-intact KEAP1/NFE2L2, and low-TMB MSI/WRN. Existing active untested claims remain H263 EMT-low PTEN/STAT3, H270 MTAP-loss CDKN2A/MDM2, H271 KEAP1/NFE2L2 STK11 interaction, H272 MSI/WRN high-TMB interaction. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable."
